  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 254 AM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nThe upper level trough will move off to the east on Friday.\nHighs on Friday are expected to range from the middle 40s across\ncentral Missouri to the middle 50s across extreme southeastern\nKansas and far western Missouri. An upper level ridge will move\nover the region on Saturday with highs in the 50s into the 60s \nexpected. \n\nAn upper level trough will then move east across the region \nSaturday night and Sunday and will bring some rain chances to \nthe area. There are difference between the models on the track\nof the system, with some keeping the better lift to the north \nof the area while others bringing it south across the entire \narea. Warmer temperatures will be in place so rain will occur \nwith this system. If the further northern track occurs, much of \nthe area may remain dry, but if the more southern track occurs \nlight rain will be possible across much of the area. At this \ntime rainfall chances range from 50% across the northern \nportions of the area to 20% across far southern Missouri. \n\nUpper level ridging will move east towards the area early next\nweek with highs in the 50s to lower 60s expected.",
